    <item>
      <title>NDES guidance adds SID certificate request settings and validation safeguards — 7 November 2026</title>
      <link>https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 07 Nov 2026 08:15:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <description><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 7 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">NDES guidance adds SID certificate request settings and validation safeguards</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">A new AD CS article explains how to configure NDES to accept SID information in certificate requests through registry settings for SAN URI and NTDS CA security extension formats.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/assets/products/ad-cs.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">AD CS · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/#doc-2026-11-07-configure-ndes-for-sid-certificate-requests-in-windows-server-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">New AD CS guidance covers SID-enabled NDES requests</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The article documents registry configuration for accepting SID information in certificate requests, including SAN URI and NTDS CA security extension formats. It advises that a trusted component validate the SID before enabling these settings and specifies resetting IIS or restarting NDES to apply changes.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 7 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></description>
      <content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="max-width:760px;color:#11181d;font-family:Arial,sans-serif"><div style="margin:0 0 24px"><div style="margin:0 0 6px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.3 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase">Day in brief · 7 November 2026</div><h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;font:650 28px/1.2 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">NDES guidance adds SID certificate request settings and validation safeguards</a></h2><p style="margin:0;color:#263030;font:16px/1.6 Arial,sans-serif">A new AD CS article explains how to configure NDES to accept SID information in certificate requests through registry settings for SAN URI and NTDS CA security extension formats.</p></div><div style="margin:0 0 20px;padding:0 0 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8d3c7"><table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0" style="width:100%;border:0;border-collapse:collapse"><tr><td width="46" valign="top" style="width:46px;min-width:46px;padding:1px 8px 0 0;vertical-align:top;white-space:nowrap"><img src="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/assets/products/ad-cs.svg" width="20" height="20" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:20px!important;max-width:20px!important;height:20px!important;max-height:20px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"><span style="display:inline-block;width:5px"></span><img src="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/assets/topics/general.svg" width="16" height="16" alt="" style="display:inline-block;width:16px!important;max-width:16px!important;height:16px!important;max-height:16px!important;object-fit:contain;vertical-align:middle"></td><td valign="top" style="padding:0;vertical-align:top"><div style="margin:0 0 5px;color:#0d5745;font:700 11px/1.35 Arial,sans-serif;letter-spacing:.04em;text-transform:uppercase">AD CS · General</div><h3 style="margin:0 0 7px;font:600 18px/1.3 Georgia,serif"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/#doc-2026-11-07-configure-ndes-for-sid-certificate-requests-in-windows-server-01" style="color:#11181d;text-decoration:none">New AD CS guidance covers SID-enabled NDES requests</a></h3></td></tr></table><p style="margin:5px 0 0;color:#46514e;font:14px/1.55 Arial,sans-serif">The article documents registry configuration for accepting SID information in certificate requests, including SAN URI and NTDS CA security extension formats. It advises that a trusted component validate the SID before enabling these settings and specifies resetting IIS or restarting NDES to apply changes.</p></div><p style="margin:24px 0 0"><a href="https://daily.windowsserver.admin.news/day/2026-11-07/" style="color:#0d5745;font:700 15px/1.4 Georgia,serif">View all updates for 7 November 2026 →</a></p></div>]]></content:encoded>
    </item>
